Before you adopt — what this records

Your adoption creates a public record containing:
- the name or pseudonym you give us;
- the date of adoption;
- a public reference number (for example UPD-2026-0001);
- a cryptographic hash of those facts, so anyone can verify them.

That record is permanent and public. It is the point of the ledger: anyone can check that your adoption is real and has not been altered. Because the record is cryptographically signed, copies may be held by others, and we cannot recall them — so please read what erasure means here (/privacy) before you continue.

You may adopt under a pseudonym. Give the name you wish to appear on the ledger; it does not have to be your legal name. If we hold any link between a pseudonym and a real identity, we keep it privately and never publish it.

Full detail is in our Privacy Notice (/privacy). For access, correction, erasure, or to withdraw consent: privacy@primedirective.dev (mailto:privacy@primedirective.dev).

I have read the above. I consent to my adoption being recorded permanently and publicly on the ledger as described.
